1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
Welcome to Topic 2.

2
00:00:01,850 --> 00:00:03,450
1, Roles and Features.

3
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:10,100
Your servers have names and addresses now,
but they do not do any real work yet.

4
00:00:10,350 --> 00:00:14,750
To give a server a job, you add roles and
features.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,800
In this video you will learn the
difference between roles, role services

6
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:21,250
and features.

7
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:27,900
You will walk through the Add Roles and
Features Wizard page by page, and see how

8
00:00:28,150 --> 00:00:29,750
to remove things again.

9
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Then you will do the same with PowerShell,
install a feature whose files are missing,

10
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:38,250
and work on Server Core.

11
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,500
Let's sort out three words.

12
00:00:40,750 --> 00:00:45,550
A role is a main job the server does for
other computers.

13
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:48,600
DNS Server and DHCP Server are roles.

14
00:00:48,850 --> 00:00:55,250
A role service is one part of a role that
you can add on its own.

15
00:00:55,500 --> 00:01:02,300
For example, File and Storage Services is
a role, and File Server is one of its role

16
00:01:02,550 --> 00:01:03,750
services.

17
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:11,600
A feature is a tool that supports the
server or a role, but it is not a job for

18
00:01:11,850 --> 00:01:13,050
others.

19
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:14,900
Windows Server Backup, .

20
00:01:15,150 --> 00:01:16,350
NET Framework 3.

21
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:19,000
5 and Telnet Client are features.

22
00:01:19,250 --> 00:01:21,650
You have two tools for this.

23
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:27,100
On a Desktop Experience server, Server
Manager has the Add Roles and Features

24
00:01:27,350 --> 00:01:28,550
Wizard.

25
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:35,200
It shows every role and feature as a check
box, adds management tools by default, and

26
00:01:35,450 --> 00:01:38,250
asks about anything your choice depends
on.

27
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:41,700
PowerShell does the same with three
cmdlets: Get-WindowsFeature,

28
00:01:41,950 --> 00:01:43,150
Install-WindowsFeature and
Uninstall-WindowsFeature.

29
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:46,600
PowerShell works on Server Core and in
scripts.

30
00:01:46,850 --> 00:01:51,650
One detail: the wizard shows display
names, like Windows Server Backup, while

31
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:54,300
PowerShell uses short names, like
Windows-Server-Backup.

32
00:01:54,550 --> 00:01:59,750
To start the wizard, open Server Manager,
select Manage, then Add Roles and

33
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,200
Features.

34
00:02:01,450 --> 00:02:05,050
The first page, Before You Begin, is a
reminder.

35
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:10,500
Check that the Administrator password is
strong, the address is static, and updates

36
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:11,950
are current.

37
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:15,400
You can tick Skip this page by default.

38
00:02:15,650 --> 00:02:17,250
Next comes Installation Type.

39
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:19,500
Choose Role-based or feature-based
installation.

40
00:02:19,750 --> 00:02:23,750
That is the right choice for everything in
this course.

41
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:28,800
The other option, Remote Desktop Services
installation, is only for building a

42
00:02:29,050 --> 00:02:30,250
Remote Desktop deployment.

43
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:33,700
On Server Selection you choose where to
install.

44
00:02:33,950 --> 00:02:37,150
Keep Select a server from the server pool.

45
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:41,800
The server pool lists the servers that
this Server Manager manages.

46
00:02:42,050 --> 00:02:45,250
Right now that is only SRV01, with 192.

47
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:46,700
168.

48
00:02:46,950 --> 00:02:48,150
50.

49
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,600
20.

50
00:02:49,850 --> 00:02:52,650
Select it, and the wizard installs there.

51
00:02:52,900 --> 00:02:58,900
The other option, Select a virtual hard
disk, adds roles to an offline VHD file,

52
00:02:59,150 --> 00:03:02,350
which is handy when you prepare virtual
machines.

53
00:03:02,600 --> 00:03:03,800
In Topic 2.

54
00:03:04,050 --> 00:03:10,450
3 you will add SRV-CORE to the pool, so
you can target it from here too.

55
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:14,700
The Server Roles page lists the roles with
check boxes.

56
00:03:14,950 --> 00:03:18,550
Notice File and Storage Services is
already partly installed.

57
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,400
Every server has it.

58
00:03:20,650 --> 00:03:25,050
When you select a role, like DNS Server, a
pop-up appears.

59
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:29,300
It asks: Add features that are required
for DNS Server?

60
00:03:29,550 --> 00:03:33,550
It lists the management tools, such as DNS
Server Tools.

61
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:37,400
Keep Include management tools checked and
select Add Features.

62
00:03:37,650 --> 00:03:42,050
If you select Cancel instead, the role
check box clears again.

63
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:47,900
The tools do not have to be on the same
server as the role.

64
00:03:48,150 --> 00:03:50,150
Next is the Features page.

65
00:03:50,400 --> 00:03:56,000
The list is long and it scrolls, so the
slide shows a short version.

66
00:03:56,250 --> 00:03:57,850
Two features matter today.

67
00:03:58,100 --> 00:04:02,900
Windows Server Backup is the one you add
in Lab Part 2.

68
00:04:03,150 --> 00:04:04,350
And .

69
00:04:04,600 --> 00:04:05,800
NET Framework 3.

70
00:04:06,050 --> 00:04:10,850
5 is special: its files are not on the
server at all.

71
00:04:11,100 --> 00:04:14,300
You will see the fix in a moment.

72
00:04:14,550 --> 00:04:18,150
Also, some roles add their own pages after
Features.

73
00:04:18,400 --> 00:04:21,600
DNS Server, for example, adds an
information page.

74
00:04:21,850 --> 00:04:24,250
Read those pages, then select Next.

75
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:27,700
The Confirmation page lists what will be
installed.

76
00:04:27,950 --> 00:04:32,750
There is a check box called Restart the
destination server automatically if

77
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,200
required.

78
00:04:34,450 --> 00:04:39,250
Leave it clear in the labs, so you decide
when to restart.

79
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:40,700
For .

80
00:04:40,950 --> 00:04:42,150
NET 3.

81
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:48,800
5 you also get a yellow warning: Do you
need to specify an alternate source path?

82
00:04:49,050 --> 00:04:54,250
Select the link Specify an alternate
source path, and type D colon backslash

83
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:55,700
sources backslash sxs.

84
00:04:55,950 --> 00:05:02,750
That folder is on the Windows Server ISO,
which is attached as drive D in your pod.

85
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,200
Then select Install.

86
00:05:04,450 --> 00:05:07,250
The Results page shows a progress bar.

87
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:13,500
When it finishes, it says Installation
succeeded on SRV01, or it tells you that a

88
00:05:13,750 --> 00:05:14,950
restart is needed.

89
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:20,000
Here is a nice detail: you can select
Close at any time.

90
00:05:20,250 --> 00:05:23,050
The installation keeps running in the
background.

91
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:28,900
To check on it later, select the
Notifications flag at the top of Server

92
00:05:29,150 --> 00:05:30,350
Manager.

93
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:35,800
It shows the feature installation task,
and Task Details opens the full progress

94
00:05:36,050 --> 00:05:37,250
again.

95
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:40,700
So the wizard never forces you to wait.

96
00:05:40,950 --> 00:05:43,750
Removing works the same way, in reverse.

97
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:48,000
In Server Manager, select Manage, then
Remove Roles and Features.

98
00:05:48,250 --> 00:05:51,850
The pages are almost the same, without
Installation Type.

99
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:58,100
On the Features page, clear the check box
of the feature you want to remove.

100
00:05:58,350 --> 00:06:00,350
A cleared box means remove.

101
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:07,400
If other roles or features depend on it, a
pop-up asks whether to remove them too, so

102
00:06:07,650 --> 00:06:09,250
read that list carefully.

103
00:06:09,500 --> 00:06:11,500
Then on Confirmation, select Remove.

104
00:06:11,750 --> 00:06:16,950
The same restart check box is there, and
the same Results page follows.

105
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:18,400
Now PowerShell.

106
00:06:18,650 --> 00:06:20,650
Get-WindowsFeature lists roles and
features.

107
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:26,900
Use dash Name with wildcards to filter, or
pipe it to Where-Object Installed to see

108
00:06:27,150 --> 00:06:28,750
only what is installed.

109
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:35,400
Read the brackets: an X means installed,
and an indented line is a role service or

110
00:06:35,650 --> 00:06:36,850
subfeature.

111
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:38,700
Then read Install State.

112
00:06:38,950 --> 00:06:42,950
Available means the files are on the
server and ready.

113
00:06:43,200 --> 00:06:48,800
Removed means the files are not on the
server, so you need a source.

114
00:06:49,050 --> 00:06:53,450
And InstallPending or UninstallPending
means a restart is needed to finish.

115
00:06:53,700 --> 00:06:55,300
Install-WindowsFeature installs by name.

116
00:06:55,550 --> 00:06:59,950
Add dash IncludeManagementTools, because
PowerShell does not add the tools unless

117
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:01,400
you ask.

118
00:07:01,650 --> 00:07:03,250
Try dash WhatIf first.

119
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:08,300
It shows the plan and installs nothing, so
Restart Needed says Maybe.

120
00:07:08,550 --> 00:07:10,550
Then run it for real.

121
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,800
The result has four columns.

122
00:07:13,050 --> 00:07:18,650
Success True, Restart Needed No, Exit Code
Success, and Feature Result lists what was

123
00:07:18,900 --> 00:07:20,100
installed.

124
00:07:20,350 --> 00:07:24,350
Run it again and you get NoChangeNeeded
with empty braces.

125
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:26,600
That is not an error.

126
00:07:26,850 --> 00:07:30,050
The feature was already there, so nothing
changed.

127
00:07:30,300 --> 00:07:33,100
Where does Windows find a feature's files?

128
00:07:33,350 --> 00:07:36,550
First in the local store, the WinSxS
folder.

129
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:42,400
Second in the path you give with dash
Source, or the wizard's alternate path.

130
00:07:42,650 --> 00:07:46,250
Third in a repair source set by Group
Policy.

131
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:47,700
Last, Windows Update.

132
00:07:47,950 --> 00:07:51,550
Our pod has no internet, so step four
fails.

133
00:07:51,800 --> 00:07:53,000
.

134
00:07:53,250 --> 00:07:54,450
NET 3.

135
00:07:54,700 --> 00:08:01,500
5 is in the Removed state on a standard
install, so give it dash Source D colon

136
00:08:01,750 --> 00:08:03,350
backslash sources backslash sxs.

137
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:09,600
Without it, an offline server fails with
an error that the source files could not

138
00:08:09,850 --> 00:08:11,050
be found.

139
00:08:11,300 --> 00:08:14,900
To remove a feature, use
Uninstall-WindowsFeature with the same

140
00:08:15,150 --> 00:08:17,550
name you used to install it.

141
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:21,800
You get the same result object, so read
Restart Needed.

142
00:08:22,050 --> 00:08:24,850
Yes means you must restart to finish.

143
00:08:25,100 --> 00:08:27,100
Afterwards, Get-WindowsFeature shows
Available again.

144
00:08:27,350 --> 00:08:33,350
The files stay on the server, so you can
reinstall any time without a source.

145
00:08:33,600 --> 00:08:36,400
There is also a dash Remove parameter.

146
00:08:36,650 --> 00:08:41,450
It deletes the files from WinSxS too, and
the state becomes Removed.

147
00:08:41,700 --> 00:08:46,900
It saves disk space, but we do not use it
in this course.

148
00:08:47,150 --> 00:08:53,150
Server Core has no Server Manager window,
so there is no wizard at the console.

149
00:08:53,400 --> 00:08:58,200
Instead, at the SRV-CORE console, choose
option fifteen in SConfig to open

150
00:08:58,450 --> 00:08:59,650
PowerShell.

151
00:08:59,900 --> 00:09:01,900
Then use the same cmdlets.

152
00:09:02,150 --> 00:09:05,750
Check with Get-WindowsFeature, install
with Install-WindowsFeature, and read the

153
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,400
result object exactly the same way.

154
00:09:08,650 --> 00:09:09,850
In Topic 2.

155
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:16,100
3 you will also manage SRV-CORE from
Server Manager on SRV01, so the wizard can

156
00:09:16,350 --> 00:09:17,550
target it remotely.

157
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:23,000
And remember, features that need the
desktop are not offered on Server Core.

158
00:09:23,250 --> 00:09:25,250
Here are four common mistakes.

159
00:09:25,500 --> 00:09:26,700
One: installing .

160
00:09:26,950 --> 00:09:28,150
NET 3.

161
00:09:28,400 --> 00:09:31,600
5 with no source on an offline server.

162
00:09:31,850 --> 00:09:35,850
It fails, so give the D colon sources sxs
path.

163
00:09:36,100 --> 00:09:39,300
Two: expecting PowerShell to add the
management tools.

164
00:09:39,550 --> 00:09:41,950
It only does with dash
IncludeManagementTools.

165
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:44,200
Three: calling NoChangeNeeded an error.

166
00:09:44,450 --> 00:09:48,450
Success is still True, the feature was
simply already installed.

167
00:09:48,700 --> 00:09:50,700
Four: ignoring Restart Needed Yes.

168
00:09:50,950 --> 00:09:56,550
The change is not finished until you
restart, so plan the restart and then

169
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:59,600
check the Install State again with
Get-WindowsFeature.

170
00:09:59,850 --> 00:10:01,450
Time to check yourself.

171
00:10:01,700 --> 00:10:05,700
Imagine a classmate is busy adding
features in the pod.

172
00:10:05,950 --> 00:10:11,950
First, is Windows Server Backup a role, a
role service or a feature, and why?

173
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:14,600
Second, Get-WindowsFeature shows
NET-Framework-Core as Removed.

174
00:10:14,850 --> 00:10:16,850
What does the install need?

175
00:10:17,100 --> 00:10:19,500
Third, Install-WindowsFeature returns
True, No, NoChangeNeeded.

176
00:10:19,750 --> 00:10:20,950
What happened?

177
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:26,400
And fourth, they installed DNS Server with
PowerShell, but the DNS console is

178
00:10:26,650 --> 00:10:27,850
missing.

179
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:30,100
What did they leave out?

180
00:10:30,350 --> 00:10:35,550
Pause the video now, think about your
answers, maybe write them down, then

181
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:37,000
continue.

182
00:10:37,250 --> 00:10:38,850
Here are the answers.

183
00:10:39,100 --> 00:10:41,900
One: Windows Server Backup is a feature.

184
00:10:42,150 --> 00:10:47,750
It supports the server itself and is not a
service that other computers use.

185
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:53,200
Two: it needs a source, dash Source D
colon backslash sources backslash sxs,

186
00:10:53,450 --> 00:10:59,050
because the files are not on the server
and the pod has no internet.

187
00:10:59,300 --> 00:11:01,300
Three: it was already installed.

188
00:11:01,550 --> 00:11:04,750
Success is True, and nothing needed to
change.

189
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,400
Four: they left out dash
IncludeManagementTools.

190
00:11:07,650 --> 00:11:12,050
The wizard adds the tools by default, but
PowerShell does not.

191
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:13,500
I'm on SRV01.

192
00:11:13,750 --> 00:11:14,950
First, PowerShell.

193
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:18,800
Get-WindowsFeature shows Windows Server
Backup as Available and .

194
00:11:19,050 --> 00:11:20,250
NET 3.

195
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:21,700
5 as Removed.

196
00:11:21,950 --> 00:11:25,150
Now Server Manager, Manage, Add Roles and
Features.

197
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:27,000
Role-based, SRV01, no roles.

198
00:11:27,250 --> 00:11:30,850
On Features I tick Windows Server Backup
and .

199
00:11:31,100 --> 00:11:32,300
NET Framework 3.

200
00:11:32,550 --> 00:11:33,750
5.

201
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,800
Here is the yellow warning on
Confirmation.

202
00:11:37,050 --> 00:11:42,250
I select Specify an alternate source path,
type D colon backslash sources backslash

203
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:44,900
sxs, and select OK, then Install.

204
00:11:45,150 --> 00:11:48,350
I can close the wizard while it runs.

205
00:11:48,600 --> 00:11:51,000
The Notifications flag shows the task.

206
00:11:51,250 --> 00:11:52,450
Done.

207
00:11:52,700 --> 00:11:55,900
Back in PowerShell, both features now show
Installed.

208
00:11:56,150 --> 00:12:01,750
To wrap up: roles serve other computers,
role services are parts of roles, and

209
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,600
features support the server.

210
00:12:03,850 --> 00:12:08,250
The wizard goes through Installation Type,
Server Selection, Server Roles, Features

211
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:09,700
and Confirmation.

212
00:12:09,950 --> 00:12:13,150
In PowerShell, Get-WindowsFeature shows
the state, Install-WindowsFeature adds,

213
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:14,600
and Uninstall-WindowsFeature removes.

214
00:12:14,850 --> 00:12:16,850
Removed features need a source.

215
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:18,300
In Lab 2.

216
00:12:18,550 --> 00:12:24,950
1 you explore SRV01, add features with the
wizard and from the ISO, work on SRV-CORE

217
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:27,200
with PowerShell, and remove features.

218
00:12:27,450 --> 00:12:29,450
About forty-five minutes, practice only.

219
00:12:29,700 --> 00:12:31,700
See you in the lab.
